# # BDD `step` scenario marker
#
# **Feature IDs:** #SPEC-STEP
# **Category:** Testing
# **Status:** Implemented
#
# ## Overview
#
# `step(description)` is the manual-only scenario marker consumed by
# spipe-docgen. It is a pure no-op at run time. Regression guard: the
# interpreted BDD path used to raise
# `semantic: function `step` not found` for every example calling it,
# which failed 222 of the 377 app/os specs in the 2026-08-31 suite.

describe "spec step marker":
    it "resolves and is a no-op":
        step("Verify: step() resolves in the interpreted BDD path")
        var seen = 0
        seen = seen + 1
        expect(seen).to_equal(1)

    it "accepts an empty description":
        step("")
        expect(true).to_equal(true)

    it "does not perturb example counting":
        step("first")
        step("second")
        step("third")
        expect(3).to_equal(3)
